# S1 pilot — material read gate: REST route + lib/ai/embedding.ts (hybrid + SQL RAG branches).
# See docs/PICT_CENSUS.md § S1 for the oracle spec (tests/models/material-visibility.oracle.ts).
#
# `Path` (rest / rag-hybrid / rag-sql) is deliberately NOT a dimension here: as a PICT factor it
# would route each row to exactly one implementation, so no row would ever compare two paths on
# the same input — the opposite of a drift contract. Instead every row generated from this model
# is exercised against all three paths in the world-builder
# (apps/core/app/tests/integration/material-visibility.integration.test.ts), which cross-products
# Path itself.
Role:              ADMIN, UNIT_ADMIN, INSTRUCTOR, TA, STUDENT, ANON
Enrolled:          yes, no
VisibleToStudents: true, false
AvailableAt:       past, future, null
Deleted:           yes, no
Unpublished:       yes, no

IF [Role] in {"ADMIN", "UNIT_ADMIN", "ANON"} THEN [Enrolled] = "no";
